From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 02 Feb 2026 10:06:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: allow on-channel scan for DFS channels

If a link needs radar detection, mac80211 allows a scan on the radio
of that link only if the region allows pre-CAC and no CAC runs. A
scan of only the operating channel of that link does not leave the
channel, so this restriction does not apply to it.

The exemption does not apply while that link runs a CAC. A CAC needs
radar detection without a gap, and a driver can stop its detector for
the scan dwell, also on the operating channel.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 net/mac80211/chan.c |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/net/mac80211/chan.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/chan.c
@@ -966,6 +966,10 @@ bool ieee80211_is_radar_required(struct
 	for_each_sdata_link(local, link) {
 		if (link->radar_required) {
 			chan = link->conf->chanreq.oper.chan;
+
+			if (req->n_channels == 1 && req->channels[0] == chan &&
+			    !link->sdata->wdev.links[link->link_id].cac_started)
+				continue;
 			radio_idx = cfg80211_get_radio_idx_by_chan(wiphy, chan);
 
 			if (ieee80211_is_radio_idx_in_scan_req(wiphy, req,
